; A tag assertion is re-marked uncompiled before every check, so its
; accumulator must keep counting across the checks: the third tagged
; transaction is the first to see n = 3 and fails the assertion.

tag Seq
    assert (n = n + 1; n < 3)

2024/01/05 * Grocery
    ; Seq: a
    Expenses:Food                  $50.00
    Assets:Checking

2024/01/10 * Coffee
    ; Seq: b
    Expenses:Food                   $5.00
    Assets:Checking

2024/01/12 * Tea
    ; Seq: c
    Expenses:Food                   $3.00
    Assets:Checking

test reg -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 21:
While checking transaction metadata from "$FILE", lines 18-21:
> 2024/01/12 * Tea
>     ; Seq: c
>     Expenses:Food                   $3.00
>     Assets:Checking
Error: Metadata assertion failed for (Seq: c): (n = (n + {1}); (n < {3}))
end test
